    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0846" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.156/36</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Denning</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to previous
                    correspondence relative to the Tangier port concession. There are transmitted
                    herewith, for your information, two copies of an instruction, dated September
                    21, 1922, which the American Chargé d’Affaires at Paris delivered to the French
                    Government on October 6, 1922.<anchor n="10a" xml:id="d633-f1"/></p>
                <p>You are requested to hand a copy of this communication to the Vizier of the
                    Sultan of Morocco at Tangier and to inform him that, as this Government has now
                    taken up the matter of the port concession direct with the French Government
                    through the American Embassy at Paris, no further reply will be made to his note
                    of July 6, 1922.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d633-f2"/> You may point out, however,
                    that this Government’s views in regard to the note in question are fully stated
                    in the enclosed instruction.</p>
                <p>You are further informed that the purport of this instruction will be conveyed
                    verbally to the diplomatic representatives at Washington of France, Great
                    Britain, Spain, Belgium, Italy, the Netherlands, Portugal and Sweden.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
